Sanc37/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MaxiSanc37/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T13:02:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T13:02:36Z","body":"\r\nWarp at viewport edge\r\n\r\nWindows | ✅ Works (SetCursorPos)\r\nLinux — native Wayland (wp-pointer-warp-v1, recent Mutter) | ✅ Works\r\nLinux — X11 / XWayland | ❌ Cursor warp is ignored during active pointer motion\r\n\r\nImportantly, the X11/XWayland limitation is not introduced by this PR — it equally affects the pre-existing warped mouse panning feature, since both go through **Input::warp_mouse**. On platforms where cursor warping is supported (Windows and native Wayland), tablet/trackpad navigation now warps correctly across all viewport edges.\r\n\r\nI had to re-work the PR since there were new changes in the main branch and it had introduced some merge conflicts. In-between I changed to Ubuntu 26.04 LTS and I happened to find that the warp fix I did on Windows wasn't working properly. Now everything works as intended and all changes are ready to be merged.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4958228458/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]